---
/* ============================================================================
   Brief.astro — the short intro, right after the hero.
   ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
   Round 4 moved the mesh portrait into the hero and dropped the "About"
   eyebrow — a single readable column reads more like a person talking than a
   résumé section. Round 5 removed the stats counters. Round 6: Jayson's own
   rewrite of the paragraph, set bigger, and the section fills one screen
   (.v3-screen, v3.css). Keeps `id="about"`: other docs reference the anchor.

   Size (rounds 7–8): two levels of display type that together fill one
   screen. "Hi, I'm Jayson." is the headline (≈47px phones → 114px wide);
   the paragraph runs at about half that (≈28px → 58px) at a 24ch measure —
   display text reads best at roughly 20–30 characters a line, which lands it
   on 7–8 lines. The words ink in on scroll from a near-invisible ghost
   ([data-ink], v3-motion.ts / v3.css .v3-word).
   ========================================================================= */
---

<section id="about" class="v3-brief v3-screen container" aria-labelledby="v3-brief-title">
  <div class="v3-brief__body">
    <h2 id="v3-brief-title" data-split>Hi, I'm Jayson.</h2>
    <p class="v3-brief__text" data-ink>
      I design with depth, crafting work that moves beyond surface aesthetics. By studying user
      perception, I build visual layers that deliver immediate impact at first glance and deeper
      discovery on the second.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  /* --space-l, not --space-section: the two big type levels already fill the
     screen, and the larger padding pushed the section past one viewport. */
  .v3-brief {
    padding-block: var(--space-l);
  }

  .v3-brief__body {
    display: grid;
    justify-items: center;
    text-align: center;
  }

  /* The greeting is the headline, in the sans (round 8 — he didn't want the
     serif here); round 9 took it down a notch, to ≈41px phones → 96px wide,
     still well above the paragraph. */
  .v3-brief h2 {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: clamp(2.5rem, 1.3rem + 5.2vw, 6rem);
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: -0.035em;
    line-height: 1;
  }

  .v3-brief__text {
    font-size: clamp(1.75rem, 1.1rem + 2.8vw, 3.5rem);
    font-weight: 500;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    line-height: 1.15;
    max-inline-size: 24ch;
    margin-block: var(--space-m) 0;
    text-wrap: pretty;
  }
</style>
